# Water systems' controls wiped through a shared remote-support platform: Juneau, Alaska
variant "Juneau, Alaska"
    summary "An AI agent wipes the controls of the water system of Juneau, Alaska through the remote-support
        platform of the OT integrator that it uses."
    scope "The people that the water system of Juneau, Alaska serves, the hospitals that it supplies and the
        businesses that need public water there."

juneau: Utility
    "City and Borough of Juneau, Alaska. Its ID in the federal inventory is AK2110342."
    title "Juneau"
    let buys = []
    let sells = []
    name = "Juneau"
    demand = 4.7619 Mgal/day  @juneau_demand
    nameplate = 5.024 Mgal/day  @juneau_nameplate
    storage = 11 Mgal  @juneau_storage
    bought = 0 Mgal/day  @juneau_bought
    sold = 0 Mgal/day  @juneau_sold
    va_rate = 461317.55 USD2025/h  @juneau_va_rate

juneau_homes: Households
    "The people that Juneau serves."
    title "Juneau: homes"
    let utility = juneau
    population = 38526 people  @juneau_homes_population

juneau_hospitals: Hospitals
    "The hospital that Juneau supplies: Bartlett Regional Hospital."
    title "Juneau: hospitals"
    let utility = juneau
    name = "Juneau"
    facilities = 1 facilities  @juneau_hospitals_facilities

notes:
    limitations:
        thin-margin: "On its peak day Juneau produces 5.024 Mgal against a need of 5.0 Mgal, so its stored
            water refills at almost nothing after an outage. The city met its peaks by cutting its sales to
            cruise ships, which the model cannot do, so the interruption can be longer here than in
            fact."  @juneau_nameplate
        wellfield: "No rated capacity of the wellfield was found; its 3.024 Mgal a day is one reading from
            2014, before a planned expansion. If the wellfield gives more today, the system recovers faster in
            fact than here."  @juneau_nameplate
    verification:
        research: "variants/juneau/evidence/research.md"

record juneau_demand: assumption A-SC43-PEAK-DAY "In the summer of 2013 the utility's daily output spiked to
    five million gallons a day, against an average of 3.5 million, a peak ratio of 1.42857. CBJ sells no water
    to other systems, so the demand is 5.0 / 1.05 = 4.7619 MGD. The peak includes the water sold to cruise
    ships, which are customers, not water systems; that summer they were held to 200,000 gallons a day in
    all."
    claims:
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-PEAK
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-DELIVERED
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-SUPPLY

record juneau_nameplate: source "The sum of the two sources: the Last Chance Basin wellfield, which at full
    pumping in May 2014 drew about 2,100 gallons a minute (3.024 MGD), and the Salmon Creek membrane
    filtration plant, rated at 2 MGD: 5.024 MGD. The utility superintendent gave the system a design capacity
    of five million gallons a day in 2013. No source gives a rated capacity for the wellfield."
    claims:
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-LCB-OUTPUT
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-PLANTS
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-PEAK
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-SUPPLY

record juneau_storage: source "The 2012 draft supply plan gives 7 water reservoirs that store 11 million
    gallons. The system now counts 9 reservoirs (6 reservoirs and 3 contact tanks on the CBJ page), but no
    later volume is published. The plan does not say whether the 3.2 million gallons of the Mill Tunnel are
    part of the 11 million."
    claims:
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-STORAGE
            datum: reservoir_storage
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-PLANTS
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-DELIVERED

record juneau_bought: source "CBJ draws all its water from its own two sources, the Last Chance Basin
    wellfield and Salmon Creek; no source names a purchase from another water system."
    claims:
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-SUPPLY
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-PLANTS

record juneau_sold: source "No source names a sale to another water system. CBJ sells water to cruise ships
    (on average about 61 million gallons a year), but they are customers, so their water stays in the demand."
    claims:
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-PEAK
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-SUPPLY
        E-SC43-JUNEAU-CBJ-SC-OUTAGE

record juneau_homes_population: assumption A-SC43-REACH "SDWIS federal data list 38,526 people served by
    Juneau (AK2110342), the system's own report through its state."
    claims:
        E-SC43-SDWIS-AK2110342
            datum: population_served

record juneau_va_rate: assumption A-SC43-ECONOMY "38,526 people served times the 2024 GDP per resident of its
    county (Juneau City and Borough, Alaska (02110): 3,226,767 thousand dollars and 31,572 people: 102,203.44
    dollars a resident) times the price factor 1.026324, over 8,760 h: 461,317.55 USD2025/h."
    claims:
        E-SC43-SDWIS-AK2110342
        E-SC43-SDWIS-COUNTIES
        E-SC43-BEA-GDP-02110
        E-SC43-BEA-POP-02110
        E-SC43-GDP-DEFLATOR

record juneau_hospitals_facilities: assumption A-SC43-HOSPITAL-JOIN "The CMS hospital list gives 1 hospital of
    the counted types whose geocoded address lies in the EPA service area of Juneau."
    claims:
        E-SC43-HOSPITALS-JUNEAU
            datum: hospitals_supplied
